Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-10-2000||04:25 PM||||I went to the first turbo site at fiero projects.com, It's a great site and it has me in lust to add a turbo to "Blue Thunder" my 87 Gt.  I called a salvage yard and they have the same turbo that he used.  I was just wondering if anyone had ANY info on turbos or installing them please send it to me. Ihave the need for speed.<P>Thanx<P>Mother||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||05-10-2000||04:36 PM||||Hey.<P>The following is knowledge gathered from a fiero that was attempted to be outfitted with a turbo and now it's only a coffe table.  <BR>The problem with that turbo setup was that the pipes running the turbo constantly broke.  Than there was the problem in persuading the computer to understand what boost means.  Add to all this the inherent heat that is generated by the turbo and the position of the engine in a fiero not the best cooling system out there.  If you like to fix over and over again the same problem go with a turbo if you want instant power (60HP) go with a supercharger.  There is a bolt on system out there that you can put into your fiero over the weekend and a little mechanical knowhow.  If you want I'll tell you where to get the supercharger from.  My best advice is to keep away from turbos on these cars.  Your decision what you do.<P>Later<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||dman||05-10-2000||04:44 PM||||Hello Sillhouette.com.<P>Please post some info about the supercharger. I've encountered previous posts here on the forum that mentioned a few types and I'm always interested in learning about all of the different choices available to me when it comes to upgrading my fieros.<BR>Thanks in advance.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87PegasusGT||05-10-2000||06:26 PM||||LOL Silhouette jes opened a can o' worms.<BR>I can name at least 2 companies that have successful turbo setups and after doing my research, have reached the conclusion that, not only are turbos feasible, they waste alot less power and are easier to upgrade than superchargers. I intend to purchase a turbo for my 3.4 and with a couple mods, expect around 300hp.||||reg||1
