Z||000010||SCCA FIERO||05-10-2000||09:44 PM||||A supercharger takes power to make it, but a turbo takes wasted energy and makes torque. Dennis Lagura built his own turbo in his 87GT for about $800.  <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||05-11-2000||01:00 AM||||I absolutely LOVE MY TURBO!!!<BR>It's been on my car for several years, <BR>more than I can remember, with zero <BR>problems. It was bought and installed at <BR>IRM in Rockville, MD. I've got the Stage <BR>one MillerWoods turbo unit on my 51K mile <BR>86SE automatic. Anyone going to the Fiero <BR>show in Williamsburg, VA in June will see <BR>it there. <BR>I'm on my second transmission, the first <BR>one failed. The front manifold cracked, <BR>so I had both replaced with new ones, <BR>ported and polished, and finished off <BR>with Jet Hot's ceramic coating.<BR>After driving, if I open the engine <BR>compartment, I don't feel any excessive <BR>heat, nor does the car get hot. I do not <BR>have a low-temp thermostat, not a good <BR>idea. <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370</A> <P>I'm with you, 87Pegasus, someday I'd like to swap the 2.8 for the 3.4.  But, there's absolutely nothing wrong with what I've got now, and she's faster than hell!!<BR>Maybe I'll put a 3.4 in my 88 coupe, hmmmm.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
