Z||000013||MotherGoose||05-11-2000||09:59 AM||||Thanks for the info on the supercharger, however I have one problem with it.  $3200!!!<BR>And I'm doing the work, thats way to much money.  I can get a used turbo, rebuild it, and install it for a 1/4 of the money, and have the same power.  It doesn't seem cost effective.<P>Thanks<P>Mother||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shiner||05-11-2000||10:31 AM||||"why is it that most (all) pushrod engines built today are supercharged"  I don't understand what you are saying here.  You aren't saying that all f-bodies are supercharged?<P> How about the Lingenfelter (sp?) Corvette? Sequential twin turbos, twin intercoolers on a PUSHROD V8.  It does 226mph, and with the stock differential, it pulled 0-100 in something like 6.7 seconds.  What a piece of crap!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> There are advantages and disadvantages to both systems, but I think the most cost effective way to boost power to a considerable level in the 2.8 is to add a turbo.  <P> Check out the link to Dennis' page, sorry I forgot to include it.  <BR> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Racer 1||05-11-2000||11:27 AM||||Turbo's produce alot of heat and sometimes fail. Turbo produces about twice the PSI as a supercharger. Turbo's take longer to wind up where as a supercharger runs off the pulleys. You dont see any dragsters with turbos just superchargers? I have seen the turbo in the IRM catolog and it looked ugly in my opinion. With a turbo you have to get a retarder for the timing so your engine wont go <B>"BOOM</B>. I wouldnt get both just a regular engine less stuff to go wrong.||||reg||4
Z||000016||MotherGoose||05-11-2000||12:03 PM||||Guys<P>Here is what I have decided.  Everyone has strong opinions, and everyone is right.  Both systems have there merits, and with proper research and installation, they will turn our FIERO's into movin' machines.<P>The only thing I would say, is that if you don't do it yourself your going to pay a least twice what the job is worth.  There are a lot of old cars in junk yards with the parts I need, and a wealth of info on the internet.  Plus I love my FIERO, the machanic could care less.  I will do a better and cheaper job.<P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
Z||000017||87PegasusGT||05-11-2000||01:30 PM||||Racer:<BR>Not to cause problems, but A turbo can produce more psi but doesn't have to. That is why I think you can get more power. As far as retarding the timing, etc that is only neccessary on higher psi settings. You have to make similar changes with superchargers. Do you have any firsthand experience with them? How about superchargers? I only know the basics of superchargers, but I believe I am up todate on turbos.||||reg||1
